/Pg 16 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
210 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 502 0 R
/E (74LS32 \(Quad 2-Input OR\): Contains 4 independent OR gates \(used for the feedback latch\). )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
211 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 503 0 R
/E (74LS08 \(Quad 2-Input AND\): Contains 4 independent AND gates \(used to combine the logic\).)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
212 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 122 0 R
/E (Step 1: Inverting the High Sensor:- Connect the High Sensor output line to 74LS04 Pin 1 \(Input A1\).74LS04 Pin 2 \(Output Y1\) now delivers the inverted signal.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
213 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 122 0 R
/E (Step 2: Creating the Feedback Loop:- \(OR Gate\)Connect the Low Sensor output line to 74LS32 Pin 1 \(Input A1\).Connect 74LS32 Pin 2 \(Input B1\) to the final output of the circuit \(74LS08 Pin 3\). This is the crucial feedback wire that creates memory.74LS32 Pin 3 \(Output Y1\) now delivers the combined term. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
214 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 122 0 R
/E (Step 3: Combining with the Interlock:- \(AND Gate\)Connect 74LS32 Pin 3 \(OR Output\) to 74LS08 Pin 1 \(Input A1\).Connect 74LS04 Pin 2 \(NOT Output\) to 74LS08 Pin 2 \(Input B1\).74LS08 Pin 3 \(AND Output\) is your final Pump Control Signal.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
